Records only: no library code, configuration, test, notebook, digest or
generated file changes, and nothing trains on main. The maintainer's
decisions in the stance run log's lines 760 to 801 (2026-10-29 23:47
UTC to 2026-10-30 16:32 UTC), as the session's log has them in short,
in BEHAVIOR_RECIPES_PLAN §6.2 (three new rows and the dated sentence)
and the consolidation plan's §6 (the same, with each decision's
question and what it unblocks); the detail goes to the tail-habit
note's new §9 and the stance record's §29 (a later commit):

- D-D56 (00:24 and 00:45 UTC): a no-training early-bias probe, then,
  overnight and without asking again, its no-training follow-ups (the
  early-warning curve among them) and one scratch CPU training screen
  of at most 9 continuations of at most 1.5M steps from s42's
  1,048,576 checkpoint, control against one intervention on the driver
  the probe names, pinned before launch, outcome-blind, report only,
  with a durable text copy; the verified probe and follow-ups in short;
  the intervention the session chose at 04:22 UTC (critic_blind_tail3,
  the tail_3 angle hidden from the value network only); the first
  critic-blind screen's design, approval at 06:00:05 UTC and reading,
  final: line 1, not informative (the control median rise +0.09184
  against 0.10), agreed by two independent checks; its durable copy,
  claude/handoff-bias-screen, pushed at 09:17 UTC under the
  authorisation.
- D-D57 (10:23 and 12:53 UTC): the overnight report's option A, the
  screen re-run from s42's 2,097,152 checkpoint, and its launch with
  the 0.20 gate; its approval at 12:53:50 UTC and reading, final: line
  2, reduced (p 1/70; the control median rise +0.46382), agreed by two
  independent checks with wording corrections. The run log's entry is
  timed 12:54 UTC; the screen's process check puts the answer at
  12:53:09 UTC.
- D-D58 (16:23 UTC): the long critic-blind study to 12M (its build and
  criteria started at 16:32 UTC; its pin, launch and result pending),
  the second screen's durable copy (claude/handoff-bias-screen2, pushed
  at 16:26 UTC) and this records change.

Each quotes the maintainer's answer as the run log gives it. The run
log's housekeeping entries (10:24 and 16:25 UTC) decide nothing and are
in the run-log copy only. CHANGELOG Added gains one entry, and this
change's status row names the decisions.

