 | D-D53 | Taken 2026-10-29 (the maintainer's answers at 12:34, 12:42 and 13:10 UTC, after the entropy screen's reading, logged in short in the session's log): (1) the next step is the centre-of-mass follow-up the maintainer parked on 2026-10-28 at 18:40 UTC (the calibration and the regression tests of #650 revisited: absolute stance targets as strict expected failures, the calibration's ratchet, the Compsognathus robot's creep, and centre-of-mass checks on trained policies), simulation only (run by the session as four lenses, with an adversarial verifier for each measured lens, the checks on trained policies on the 24 entropy-screen end policies and their two starts); (2) at 12:42 UTC, "Yes, add the tail clamp test once policies finish": the 12 s42 end policies, every one railed, re-run deterministically with `tail_3_pitch_act`'s command held at 0, against the same policies unforced; (3) at 13:10 UTC, "Yes, include the s80 reverse test too": the 12 s80 end policies with it forced to +1. No training; exploratory and report only, not pre-registered; nothing in it changes a gate, reward, plant, task or criterion. Report only, the outcomes (verified): the railed and unrailed policies lean alike; their pitch difference was already in their starts, and their fore-aft centre-of-mass gap mostly so (the railed lineage's centre of mass moved about 5 mm back during the continuation, 11 of 12, only in the tail-up state, not shown to be the rail's doing); on the plant alone the rail moves the body's centre of mass 0.2 mm forward and 1.6 mm up, so it is no counterweight; holding it at 0 gains 63.6 reward per episode (12 of 12) and leaves the stance otherwise unchanged; forcing it on s80 costs 180 (12 of 12) and destabilises some of them; the rail persists through a learned positive feedback from the observed tail angle to the tail command (loop gain about 0.63 at the s42 ends against 0.27 at their start), whose fixed point lies past the +1 bound. The evidence is `docs/investigations/stance_2026_10/com_revisit/` and `tail_probes/`; the record is `docs/investigations/TREX_TAIL_SATURATION_HABIT_2026_10.md` (§3.6, §4.2, §4.7). |
