 with 4 per arm; the secondaries on the ledger's tail command and on the margin to the rail at the end SUPPORTED (p 1/70 each), the end loop gain NOT SUPPORTED. Two independent checks, of the statistic and of the process, agreed with no blocking finding, with wording corrections (S-2 to S-7) that the screen's report applies. Report only: two of the four controls had tail over-bar episodes within the window and no blinded run had any. From s42's mid-rise state, hiding the `tail_3` angle from the critic stopped the climb of the policy's tail command toward the rail: the most direct causal evidence so far for the critic as the climb's driver (inferred in the report); not shown from other runs or states, from the start of training or over a full run. The screen's text outputs went to an orphan branch under D-D58 (2). Screen runs certify nothing, and nothing trains on `main`. The maintainer's decisions that followed are D-D58. The evidence is `docs/investigations/stance_2026_10/bias_screen2/`; the record is `docs/investigations/TREX_TAIL_SATURATION_HABIT_2026_10.md` (§9). |
